{
  "id": "Compound::DB00898 - Gene::126",
  "verbalization": "Ethanol is implicated in the relationship with Adh1c through a shared pathway involving Alcohol Dehydrogenase (ADH) activity. The evidence suggests that Ethanol binds to Adh1a and Adh1b, both of which participate in Alcohol Dehydrogenase (ADH) activity, which is then participated by Adh1c. This indicates a potential functional link between Ethanol and Adh1c, where Ethanol may influence the activity of Adh1c through the ADH pathway. The consistent presence of Ethanol binding and ADH participation in both Adh1a and Adh1b supports the idea that Adh1c is a downstream participant in this metabolic process. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Adh1c in ethanol metabolism, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
